<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36368" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pinnĭger</span></b> , gĕra,
			gĕrum, adj.
		1. pinnagero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>feather-bearing</i>, i. e. <i>feathered</i>, <i>winged.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: pinnigero, non armigero in corpore
			tela exercentur, i. e. <i>against birds</i>, Att. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Fam. 7, 33, 1</span></i> (Trag. Rel. p. 176 Rib.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 1074</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Transf, <i>having fins</i>, <i>finny</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 963</span></i>
			; Coripp. Johann. 4, 981.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
